<ProseLayout title="Build the business system around your technical skills." description="Why Developer Business Lab publishes practical, evidence-based business systems for independent developers and technical builders." eyebrow="About Developer Business Lab"><p>Technical builders are taught how to make websites, applications, products, and infrastructure. Far less attention is given to the connected commercial systems that turn those capabilities into a durable independent business.</p><p>Developer Business Lab exists to make those systems concrete: deciding what to sell, setting a price, finding opportunities, creating useful sales conversations, validating software, reaching early customers, and operating a solo business with more discipline.</p><h2>Systems, not isolated tactics</h2><p>Each product is designed around a real operating sequence: what to learn, what to decide, what to implement, what to execute, and what evidence to use when improving it. The aim is practical implementation, not motivation, generic prompt collections, or guaranteed outcomes.</p><h2>How evidence is handled</h2><p>Claims should be traceable to documented reasoning, direct demonstrations, credible sources, or genuine product previews. Developer Business Lab does not invent testimonials, customer results, revenue figures, or certainty that the evidence cannot support.</p><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>The catalog serves freelance developers, technical consultants, solo agencies, indie developers, and bootstrapped SaaS founders who can build the technical work and now need a clearer commercial operating system around it.</p><p><Button as="a" href="/start/">Find Your Next System</Button></p></ProseLayout>
